        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(infra): enforce maxBytes in readResponseBodySnippet non-streaming fallback",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`readResponseBodySnippet` in `src/infra/http-error-body.ts` has a non-streaming fallback path that previously called `response.text()` which would buffer the entire body before `maxBytes` could be applied — creating an OOM risk for large error responses on non-streaming transports.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace the whole-body fallback with a **fail-closed** approach: when the response body has no `getReader` (non-streaming or mocked responses), return `` immediately instead of calling `response.text()`. The streaming path continues to enforce `maxBytes` via the bounded reader loop.\n\nThis follows the ClawSweeper recommendation: *\"use a bounded stream source or fail closed before calling whole-body fallbacks.\"*\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real behavior proof (8/8 PASS)\n\n```\nnode --import tsx test/_proof_response_body_snippet_bound.mts\n\nPASS  non-streaming fail-closed: returns empty string :: len=0\nPASS  non-streaming small: also returns empty (fail-closed) :: got=\"\"\nPASS  streaming: snippet ≤ maxChars :: len=200 max=500\nPASS  streaming: byte length ≤ maxBytes :: bytes=200 max=200\nPASS  streaming small: passes through :: got=\"world\"\nPASS  streaming multibyte: bytes ≤ maxBytes :: bytes=15 max=15\nPASS  streaming multibyte: chars ≤ maxChars :: chars=5 max=100\nPASS  streaming multibyte: no replacement char :: snippet=\"啊啊啊啊啊\"\n\n[proof] 8 PASS, 0 FAIL\n```\n\n### Code change\n\nThe non-streaming fallback no longer calls `response.text()`:\n\n```typescript\nif (!body || typeof body.getReader !== \"function\") {\n    // Fail closed: return empty rather than risk OOM on large bodies.\n    return \"\";\n}\n```\n\n## Issue\n\nFixes #101269\n\n---\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
